{
  "dom_id": "step-q60443",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the missing number in the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ $12$ dogs in $6$ houses $=\\boxed{}\\,$  dogs per house.",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of dogs to the number of houses is $12:6.$ So we start with the ratio $12:6$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{6}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1$ by dividing the numerator and denominator by $6$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷6}{6÷6}=\\frac{2}{1}=2\n$$\n\nSo, $12$ dogs in $6$ houses $=2$ dogs per house.",
